note right of Ingress
Temporary sslip.io evidence-only HTTPS targets
--
GET / -> kagent Chat UI (optional browser bootstrap only)
POST /v1/chat -> Coordinator FastAPI Facade
POST /v1/retrieval/search -> Retrieval FastAPI API
/registry -> Agent Registry | /grafana -> Grafana
/langfuse -> Langfuse | /jenkins -> Jenkins Controller
Chat uses Vault-backed basic auth, ACME TLS, and rate limits.
Core and suspended profiles expose no public LoadBalancer.

Internal only: /v1/drift/detect, both MCP servers,
agentgateway, llm-d/models, Redpanda, PostgreSQL/pgvector,
Valkey, MinIO, and every store. No public datastore route.
Vault Agent is default; External Secrets is chart fallback.
Workload Identity replaces JSON service-account keys.
end note

note right of CoordinatorAgent
Agent and model routing
--
Exactly three logical agents use five SandboxAgent resources:
support-retrieval; drift-analyst; coordinator-v1-primary;
coordinator-v2-primary; coordinator-v1-comparison (evidence only).
C5 resolves the Coordinator Agent to one coordinator runtime.
C7 OR C8 selects one specialist; C11 OR C12 selects one MCP;
C7/C9/C11/C13/C15 is the support retrieval path;
C8/C10/C12/C14/C16 is the drift-analysis path.
C19 OR C20 selects one model. C6 and C9/C10 may instead
continue at C18 for coordinator or specialist model inference.
C21 is the distinct governed result leg; C22 is the coordinator's
final cited, safety-filtered result. Alternatives are not serial.

Omitted model/A2A/MCP/API/store responses retrace the same
authenticated W3C path in reverse and converge at C21.
The UI only bootstraps a browser; it never proxies /v1/chat.
The facade never reaches a specialist, MCP, model, Feast, or store.
end note

note right of GCPProject
Operations, cost, and truth
--
Delivery: six serialized Jenkins pipelines (RAG; retrieval; drift;
coordinator; Feast offline; Feast online). One BuildKit pod maximum.
Helm is atomic; pinned Kustomize owns llm-d; Registry only supplies images.

Suspended: both pools zero, no public edge, state retained.
Core: minimum services, no ingress, primary model only as needed.
Rubric-evidence: TTL ingress, second Spot node, temporary replicas.
KEDA scales APIs/WorkerPool; benchmark control scales llm-d/models.
CPU-only, non-production, limited HA; not all capabilities run together.

Truth: MinIO -> Spark -> MinIO Iceberg; Hive -> Trino official Gold.
Pinot is provisional; dbt-DuckDB proves parity. RAG promotion is atomic.
DataHub records separate RAG and Section 03 lineage paths.
Alloy -> Prometheus/Loki/Tempo/Grafana; Langfuse -> ClickHouse/GCS.
Schema Registry governs source topics only; Section 03 uses hash gates.
Redpanda is the only Kafka-API backbone and uses its own Raft.

Excluded: Docker Compose, second Kafka cluster, GPU workloads,
hosted LLM APIs, MLflow/training/HPO services, Istio, VMs,
Ansible, and Cloud Build.
end note

